# wrap: wrap joints (decision C23). The chip goes in the vise legs up. The
# wire feeder feeds a jumper from pin 4 across the chip's end to pin 5,
# each end passing its pin's leg just below the tip and on past it far
# enough for 1.75 turns and a tail (wrap=). Arm A takes the wrap tool;
# at each pin, the joint presented at the iron, its bit slips over the
# leg's end, winds the wire's end round it and holds it while the iron
# solders, then its blade cuts the tail and the bit lifts off. Wound
# 1.5 turns or more, the joint holds before the solder flows.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
lift A mm=60
wire S5 awg=30 span=U1.4.tip+U1.5.tip wrap=1.75 enamel=yes
pick A W1 grasp=middle
cut S5
lift A mm=60
lay A W1
pinch P1 on=W1.1 at=1.5
release A W1
lift A mm=60
move A to=0,60,60
joints A 0 0 0 0 90 0
tool A wrapper
present U1.4+W1.1 at=S1
wrap A on=W1.1 around=U1.4 turns=1.75
touch S1 at=U1.4+W1.1 dwell=1.5 temp=400
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.4+W1.1 below=100
snip A on=W1.1
inspect U1.4+W1.1
present U1.5+W1.2 at=S1
wrap A on=W1.2 around=U1.5 turns=1.75
touch S1 at=U1.5+W1.2 dwell=1.5 temp=400
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.5+W1.2 below=100
snip A on=W1.2
inspect U1.5+W1.2
unpinch P1
inspect shorts
tool A tweezers
stage tilt=60
scope aim=U1.4+W1.1 zoom=12
